From 2023317eb0a8733b0fc49c0ba96cac12b20025c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:20:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 126/210] dt-bindings: media: amlogic,gx-vdec: VP9 is not
 available on GXBB and GXLX

The description says VDEC_HEVC decodes VP9, but GXBB and GXLX have no
VP9 support. List the SoC families that do.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
index 913d52e8bc9e..e21684ae3109 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ description: |
   - ESPARSER is a bitstream parser that outputs to a VIFIFO. Further VDEC blocks
     then feed from this VIFIFO.
   - VDEC_1 can decode MPEG-1, MPEG-2, MPEG-4 part 2, MJPEG, H.263, H.264, VC-1.
-  - VDEC_HEVC can decode HEVC and VP9.
+  - VDEC_HEVC can decode HEVC, and VP9 on GXL, GXM, G12A and SM1.
 
   Both VDEC_1 and VDEC_HEVC share the "vdec" IRQ and as such cannot run
   concurrently.
